From bc18be6c980e4561c57fec3c6920ae5e47a9526c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:45:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-5 first five data planes

Add the first five batch-5 Units on top of the source-lock tree. No guest
evidence is recorded; host catalog keeps all five planned.

- pbhub-v11 (U041-B): reuse the 0131 CONTROL_PBHUB model (single 0x61
  command space, six channel bases and the 0xFA RGB mode) and expose the
  v1.1 firmware fixture version 2; the SK6812/IAP additions documented for
  firmware v2 are represented by the shared transaction model only.
- op90 (U057): white digital-input observation on PORT.B with an
  active-low 'blocked' fixture and a raw input-level view; the exact
  output polarity and the PORT.B host availability stay catalog blockers.
- rgb-led-10cm (A035): 15-SK6812 RMT capture on the yellow PORT.B data
  line (led-rgb/led-frames/incomplete-frames); PORT.B host availability
  stays a blocker and the LED optics/power are not modeled.
- 8angle (U154): new US_ANGLE8 at 0x43 with 8x ADC12 (int16le), 8x ADC8,
  the toggle-switch byte, 9x SK6812 4-byte R,G,B,bright registers,
  firmware and address migration; the potentiometer/switch mechanics are
  NOT modeled.
- kmeter-iso-v11 (U133-V11): new US_KMETER at 0x66 exposing the
  MAX31855-derived int32le/100 Celsius and Fahrenheit values, the internal
  temperature, the ready byte, the 8-byte ASCII string views (sign + text),
  firmware and address migration. Thermocouple/isolation physics are NOT
  modeled.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest firmware) validates property
registration, fixture read/write, range/read-only rejection and the
8/15/9-element array shapes; it is not a functional PASS.

(Rebased by patch-chain reconciliation: base is the reconciled canonical chain 75f1d24 + 0120-0129 + 0131 + 0134 + 0136 + 0130 + 0133 + 0135 + 0132; this is the final layer of the canonical sequence.)
